-- ccc9-assault-officer.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), ss 270 to 270.1: assaulting a peace officer, with a weapon or causing bodily harm,
-- aggravated assault of a peace officer, consecutive sentences, disarming a peace officer.
-- LAYER 1: the law as the text states it, from no one's point of view. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled): MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: on the facts the text's words are met. JUST FALSE: the
-- text says no in its own words (here: the "who" condition of an offence section, read like an "if", reading (a): NOTES.md, Marginal readings).
-- NOTHING: not covered (an input from another part or from section 2 is itself NOTHING; the text is silent; the scope the text limits is not met).
-- Every JUST FALSE and NOTHING branch carries a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment quoting the text, or a HELPER tag where a helper of
-- ccc9-support carries an input's answer. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- SEAMS taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 3): `by s 265` (assault: ccc8), `by s 2 <term>` (section 2 terms), `by s 445.01(4)` (ccc13),
-- `s 787(1)` (the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction: ccc29).

§ `Part VIII -- Assaulting a peace officer (s 270)`

-- The facts that s 270(1) turns on. A borrowed answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN named for the section it comes from.
-- src:5032 | Assaulting a peace officer
-- src:5033 | 270 (1) Every one commits an offence who
@ref Criminal Code s 270(1) (src:5032-5033)
DECLARE `s 270(1) facts` HAS
    `the accused assaults the person, by s 265`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the person assaulted is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the person assaulted is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the officer is engaged in the execution of his duty`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person assaulted is acting in aid of such an officer`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused intends to resist or prevent the arrest or detention of himself or another person`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrest or detention is lawful`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person assaulted is engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person assaulted is making a lawful distress or seizure`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused intends to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(1)(a)
-- src:5034 | (a) assaults a public officer or peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty or a person acting in aid of such an officer;
@ref Criminal Code s 270(1)(a) (src:5034-5034)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1)(a) the accused assaults an officer in the execution of his duty or a person acting in aid of one` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST `an assault`, `an officer in the execution of duty or one aiding`)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "assaults a public officer or peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty or a person acting in aid of such an officer"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 265, s 2 public officer or s 2 peace officer is itself not covered
    WHERE
        `an assault` MEANS facts's `the accused assaults the person, by s 265`
        `an officer in the execution of duty or one aiding` MEANS
            `s 270 helper: at least one of these holds` (LIST `a public officer or peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty`, JUST (facts's `the person assaulted is acting in aid of such an officer`))
        `a public officer or peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty` MEANS
            `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST `a public officer or a peace officer`, JUST (facts's `the officer is engaged in the execution of his duty`))
        `a public officer or a peace officer` MEANS
            `s 270 helper: at least one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the person assaulted is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`, facts's `the person assaulted is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`)

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(1)(b)
-- src:5035 | (b) assaults a person with intent to resist or prevent the lawful arrest or detention of himself or another person; or
@ref Criminal Code s 270(1)(b) (src:5035-5035)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1)(b) the accused assaults a person with intent to resist or prevent a lawful arrest or detention` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the accused assaults the person, by s 265`, JUST (facts's `the accused intends to resist or prevent the arrest or detention of himself or another person`), JUST (facts's `the arrest or detention is lawful`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "assaults a person with intent to resist or prevent the lawful arrest or detention of himself or another person"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 265 is itself not covered

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(1)(c); s 270(1)(c)(i)
-- src:5036 | (c) assaults a person
-- src:5037 | (i) who is engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods or in making a lawful distress or seizure, or
@ref Criminal Code s 270(1)(c)(i) (src:5036-5037)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1)(c)(i) the accused assaults a person engaged in the lawful execution of a process or in making a lawful distress or seizure` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the accused assaults the person, by s 265`, `lawfully executing a process or making a distress or seizure`)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who is engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods or in making a lawful distress or seizure"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 265 is itself not covered
    WHERE
        `lawfully executing a process or making a distress or seizure` MEANS
            JUST (facts's `the person assaulted is engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods` OR facts's `the person assaulted is making a lawful distress or seizure`)

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(1)(c)(ii)
