-- src:5038 | (ii) with intent to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure.
@ref Criminal Code s 270(1)(c)(ii) (src:5036-5038)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1)(c)(ii) the accused assaults a person with intent to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the accused assaults the person, by s 265`, JUST (facts's `the accused intends to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with intent to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 265 is itself not covered

-- The offence of s 270(1): any one of the limbs (a), (b), (c)(i), (c)(ii). When none holds, the answer is the text's "who" no, for this section only.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(1)
-- src:5032 | Assaulting a peace officer
-- src:5033 | 270 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:5034 | (a) assaults a public officer or peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty or a person acting in aid of such an officer;
-- src:5035 | (b) assaults a person with intent to resist or prevent the lawful arrest or detention of himself or another person; or
-- src:5036 | (c) assaults a person
-- src:5037 | (i) who is engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods or in making a lawful distress or seizure, or
-- src:5038 | (ii) with intent to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure.
@ref Criminal Code s 270(1) (src:5032-5038)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270(1) the accused commits the offence of assaulting a peace officer` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: at least one of these holds` (LIST `s 270(1)(a) the accused assaults an officer in the execution of his duty or a person acting in aid of one` facts, `s 270(1)(b) the accused assaults a person with intent to resist or prevent a lawful arrest or detention` facts, `s 270(1)(c)(i) the accused assaults a person engaged in the lawful execution of a process or in making a lawful distress or seizure` facts, `s 270(1)(c)(ii) the accused assaults a person with intent to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure` facts)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb's input from another part is itself not covered

-- s 270(2): the punishment. The indictable limb states a maximum of five years. The summary-conviction limb states no penalty ("an offence
-- punishable on summary conviction"), so the penalty is the seam input from s 787(1): the general penalty for such an offence.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(2); s 270(2)(a); s 270(2)(b)
-- src:5039 | Punishment
-- src:5040 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:5041 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:5042 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 270(2) (src:5039-5042)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 270(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270(2)(a); s 270(2)(b)
-- src:5040 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:5041 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:5042 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 270(2)(a), (b) (src:5040-5042)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 270(2) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- the maximum is "a term not exceeding five years"; the limb states no minimum and no fine
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb (b) states no penalty: the answer of s 787(1), taken as an input

§ `Part VIII -- Assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm (s 270.01)`

-- src:5043 | Assaulting peace officer with weapon or causing bodily harm
-- src:5044 | 270.01 (1) Everyone commits an offence who, in committing an assault referred to in section 270,
-- src:5045 | (a) carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation of one; or
-- src:5046 | (b) causes bodily harm to the complainant.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.01(1) (src:5043-5046)
DECLARE `s 270.01(1) facts` HAS
    `the accused commits an assault referred to in section 270`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused causes bodily harm to the complainant, by s 2 bodily harm`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

