§ `Part VIII -- Aggravated assault of a peace officer (s 270.02)`

-- Offence and punishment are one sentence: "Everyone who, in committing an assault referred to in section 270, wounds, maims, disfigures or
-- endangers the life of the complainant is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years."
-- src:5051 | Aggravated assault of peace officer
-- src:5052 | 270.02 Everyone who, in committing an assault referred to in section 270, wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.02 (src:5051-5052)
DECLARE `s 270.02 facts` HAS
    `the accused commits an assault referred to in section 270`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the accused wounds the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused maims the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused disfigures the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused endangers the life of the complainant`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.02
-- src:5051 | Aggravated assault of peace officer
-- src:5052 | 270.02 Everyone who, in committing an assault referred to in section 270, wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.02 (src:5051-5052)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270.02 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270.02 the accused, in committing the assault, wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST facts's `the accused commits an assault referred to in section 270`, JUST (facts's `the accused wounds the complainant` OR facts's `the accused maims the complainant` OR facts's `the accused disfigures the complainant` OR facts's `the accused endangers the life of the complainant`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who, in committing an assault referred to in section 270, wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant is guilty of"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 270 assault is itself not covered

