§ `Part VIII -- Sentences to be served consecutively (s 270.03)`

-- s 270.03 is a rule for the sentencing court. For the accused it says what follows from a conviction: the sentence runs consecutively.
-- The offence is tested by section number (R1), the third condition is the answer of s 445.01(4) in another part (an input).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.03
-- src:5053 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:5054 | 270.03 A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 270(1) or 270.01(1) or section 270.02 committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.03 (src:5053-5054)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 270.03 the offence is one of subsection 270(1), subsection 270.01(1) or section 270.02` MEANS
       (offence's `section` EQUALS 270 AND offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
    OR (offence's `section` EQUALS 270.01 AND offence's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
    OR offence's `section` EQUALS 270.02

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.03
-- src:5053 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:5054 | 270.03 A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 270(1) or 270.01(1) or section 270.02 committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.03 (src:5053-5054)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), by s 445.01(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `another punishment is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270.03 the sentence shall be served consecutively to any other punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 270.03 the offence is one of subsection 270(1), subsection 270.01(1) or section 270.02` offence) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence under subsection 270(1) or 270.01(1) or section 270.02"
        IF `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), by s 445.01(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4)"
        IF `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), by s 445.01(4)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 445.01(4) is in another part
        IF NOT `another punishment is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the sentence is served consecutively to, and is silent where there is no other punishment
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the sentencing court MUST direct that the sentence be served consecutively where s 270.03 applies.
-- The text gives no time limit and no consequence for failure, so the rule carries no WITHIN and its LEST is the plain breach.
DECLARE `s 270.03 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 270.03 the court directs that the sentence be served consecutively to any other punishment`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.03
-- src:5053 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:5054 | 270.03 A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 270(1) or 270.01(1) or section 270.02 committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.03 (src:5053-5054)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), by s 445.01(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `another punishment is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 270.03 act`
`s 270.03 the sentencing court's duty to direct consecutive service` MEANS
    IF `s 270.03 the sentence shall be served consecutively to any other punishment` offence `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer, as defined in subsection 445.01(4), by s 445.01(4)` `another punishment is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 270.03 the court directs that the sentence be served consecutively to any other punishment`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 270.03: the sentence was not directed to be served consecutively"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: this is not a finding that the sentence is concurrent (the decision function answers NOTHING there)

§ `Part VIII -- Disarming a peace officer (s 270.1)`

-- src:5055 | Disarming a peace officer
-- src:5056 | 270.1 (1) Every one commits an offence who, without the consent of a peace officer, takes or attempts to take a weapon that is in the possession of the peace officer when the peace officer is engaged in the execution of his or her duty.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.1(1) (src:5055-5056)
DECLARE `s 270.1(1) facts` HAS
    `the accused takes or attempts to take a weapon`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is a weapon, by s 270.1(2)`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the weapon is in the possession of a peace officer`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the peace officer consents to the taking`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the peace officer is engaged in the execution of his or her duty`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 270.1(2): "For the purpose of subsection (1), weapon means any thing that is designed to be used to cause injury or death to, or to
-- temporarily incapacitate, a person." A "means" definition: a thing designed for none of those is the text's no.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.1(2)
-- src:5057 | Definition of weapon
-- src:5058 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), weapon means any thing that is designed to be used to cause injury or death to, or to temporarily incapacitate, a person.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.1(2) (src:5057-5058)
GIVEN `it is designed to be used to cause injury or death to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed to be used to temporarily incapacitate a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270.1(2) the thing is a weapon for the purpose of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `it is designed to be used to cause injury or death to a person` OR `it is designed to be used to temporarily incapacitate a person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "weapon means any thing that is designed to be used to cause injury or death to, or to temporarily incapacitate, a person"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.1(1)
-- src:5055 | Disarming a peace officer
-- src:5056 | 270.1 (1) Every one commits an offence who, without the consent of a peace officer, takes or attempts to take a weapon that is in the possession of the peace officer when the peace officer is engaged in the execution of his or her duty.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.1(1) (src:5055-5056)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 270.1(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 270.1(1) the accused commits the offence of disarming a peace officer` MEANS
    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST JUST (facts's `the accused takes or attempts to take a weapon`), facts's `the thing is a weapon, by s 270.1(2)`, JUST (facts's `the weapon is in the possession of a peace officer`), facts's `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`, JUST (NOT (facts's `the peace officer consents to the taking`)), JUST (facts's `the peace officer is engaged in the execution of his or her duty`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, without the consent of a peace officer, takes or attempts to take a weapon that is in the possession of the peace officer when the peace officer is engaged in the execution of his or her duty"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 peace officer is itself not covered

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.1(3); s 270.1(3)(a); s 270.1(3)(b)
-- src:5059 | Punishment
-- src:5060 | (3) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:5061 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5062 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.1(3) (src:5059-5062)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 270.1(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 270.1(3)(a); s 270.1(3)(b)
-- src:5060 | (3) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:5061 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5062 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 270.1(3)(a), (b) (src:5060-5062)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 270.1(3) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- "a term of not more than five years"; no minimum, no fine stated
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb (b) states no penalty: the answer of s 787(1), taken as an input
